{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 11: an emergency room. Patients arrive; a fixed team treats them. More arrive than leave for a while.
  How long do people wait, and how many have waited too long? }
Arrivals=
	8 + STEP(4, 6) - STEP(4, 18)
	~	patients/hour
	~	Arrivals: 8 an hour, 12 an hour between hour 6 and hour 18 (a flu outbreak).
	|
Treatment capacity=
	10
	~	patients/hour
	~	What the team can treat each hour.
	|
Treated=
	MIN(Treatment capacity, Waiting / TIME STEP + Arrivals)
	~	patients/hour
	~	Treatment: full capacity, unless there is nobody left to treat.
	|
Waiting=
	QUEUE(Arrivals, Treated, init=0)
	~	patients
	~	The waiting room: people leave oldest first.
	|
Average wait=
	WAIT(Waiting)
	~	hours
	~	How long the people in the waiting room have waited, on average.
	|
Longest wait=
	WAIT(Waiting, measure=oldest)
	~	hours
	~	How long the person who has waited longest has waited.
	|
Waiting over 2 hours=
	WAIT(Waiting, measure=count, older_than=2)
	~	patients
	~	How many have waited more than 2 hours: the number a hospital reports.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ hour ~ |
FINAL TIME = 48 ~ hour ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25 ~ hour ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.25 ~ hour ~ |
